    "lawCode": "Amd §14-0107, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2840\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to giving the\nstate soil and water conservation committee membership to the New York\nocean and Great Lakes ecosystem conservation council\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo give the State Soil and Water Conservation Committee membership to\nthe New York Ocean and Great Lakes Ecosystem Conservation Council.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 of the bill amends Subdivision 1 of Section 14-0107 of the\nEnvironmental Conservation Law, as added by Chapter 432 of the Laws\nof 2006, to allow the New York Ocean and Great Lakes Ecosystem\nConservation Council to have 10 members including the Chairman of the\nState Soil and Water Conservation Committee. Section 2 of the Bill\nprovides for an immediate effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe Ecosystem Based Management (EBM) released a report entitled \"Our\nWaters, Our Communities, Our Future.\" Included in the report was the\nrecommendation that the NYS Soil and Water Conservation Committee\nbe recognized as a full member of the NY Ocean and Great Lakes\nEcosystem Conservation Council. The SWCC provides direct guidance to\nthe 58 Soil and Water Conservation Districts (SWCDs) and has specific\nEBM principles within its legislative charge. The SWCC administers\nprograms that directly affect our natural resources, with the SWCDs\nas the local delivery system. Expanding the Council will offer a\npractical means for integration of EBM at the local level. This bill\nseeks to adopt the EBM recommendation.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nThis is a chapter amendment to Chapter 432 of the Laws of 2006 to add\nNYS Soil and Water Conservation Committee as a member of the NY Ocean\nand Great Lakes Ecosystem Conservation Council.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
