    "lawCode": "Amd §14-0107, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2840A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to giving the\nstate soil and water conservation committee membership to the New York\nocean and Great Lakes ecosystem conservation council\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo give the State Soil and Water Conservation Committee\nChairman, Commissioner of Health, Commissioner of Education and the\npresident of the environmental facilities corporation membership to\nthe New York Ocean and Great Lakes Ecosystem Conservation Council.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 of the bill amends Subdivision 1 of\nSection 14-0107 of the Environmental Conservation Law, as added by\nChapter 432 of the Laws of 2006, to allow the New York Ocean and\nGreat Lakes Ecosystem Conservation Council to have 13 members\nincluding the Chairman of the State Soil and Water Conservation\nCommittee, Commissioner of Health, Commissioner of Education and the\npresident of environmental facilities corporation. Section 2 of the\nbill provides for an immediate effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe Ecosystem Based Management (EBM)\nreleased a report\nentitled \"Our Waters, Our Communities, Our Future.\" Included in the\nreport was the recommendation that the NYS Soil and Water\nConservation Committee be recognized as a full member of the NY Ocean\nand Great Lakes Ecosystem Conservation Council. The SWCC provides\ndirect guidance to the 58 Soil and Water Conservation Districts\n(SWCDs) and has specific EBM principles within its legislative\ncharge. The SWCC administers programs that directly affect our\nnatural resources, with the SWCDs as the local delivery system.\nExpanding the Council will offer a practical means for integration of\nEBM at the local level. This bill seeks to adopt the EBM\nrecommendation.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nThis is a chapter amendment to Chapter 432 of the Laws of 2006 to add\nNYS Soil and Water Conservation Committee as a member of the NY Ocean\nand Great Lakes Ecosystem Conservation Council.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
